1
00:04:48,750 --> 00:04:54,750
Alice in Terrorland is a horror, thriller film directed by Richard John Taylor.

2
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:43,500
A recently bereaved teenage girl goes to live with her aunt in a secluded
woodland house, unaware that sinister forces lurk within.

3
00:14:26,250 --> 00:14:32,250
Alice, played by Lizzy Willis.

4
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Beth, played by Rula Lenska.

5
00:24:03,750 --> 00:24:09,750
The Mad Hatter, played by Jon-Paul Gates.

6
00:28:52,500 --> 00:28:58,500
The Rabbit, played by Steve Wraith.

7
00:33:41,250 --> 00:33:47,250
The Twins, played by Lila Sarner.

8
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
The Smoking Man, played by Nigel Troup.

9
00:43:18,750 --> 00:43:24,750
Rula Lenska (born Roza Maria Leopoldyna Lubienski 30
September 1947) is a British actress.

10
00:48:07,500 --> 00:48:13,500
She mainly appears in British stage and television productions and is known in the United
States for a series of television advertisements in the 1970s and 1980s.

11
00:52:56,250 --> 00:53:02,250
She is known for the films Queen Kong and Aura, and she portrayed
Claudia Colby in the ITV soap opera Coronation Street.

12
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:51,000
Lenska was married to the actors Brian Deacon
(1977–1987) and Dennis Waterman (1987–1998).

13
01:02:33,750 --> 01:02:39,750
Both marriages ended in divorce.

14
01:07:22,500 --> 01:07:28,500
The film explores themes of bereavement, teenage girl, independent film.

15
01:12:11,250 --> 01:12:17,250
The tone is dark and intense.
